SYNOPSIS:
           Here's a simple CLI based ute that allows most of the MAXS menu 
           functions to be used on any running MAXS node, from a CLI or 
           script.

USAGE:
           Control <NODE NUMBER> <FUNCTION>

           - <NODE NUMBER> is the node number of a running copy of MAXS BBS, 
             that you want to mess with.  eg If you have but one running 
             MAXS BBS node, then <NODE NUMBER> will be equal to one:

               Control 1 <FUNCTION>

             Similarly if you have two running MAXS BBS nodes, then you 
             would do:

               Control 1 <FUNCTION>
               Control 2 <FUNCTION>

           - <FUNCTION> is any of the following MAXS functions, if you do 
             not know what one or more of these functions do, then you better 
             stop reading this and read the DAMN MAXS manual!!!  ;-]
               LOCAL     = Local Login.
               CHAT      = Toggle Chat Enable/Disable.
               COUNTDOWN = Commence Countdown.
               TWIT      = Twit an idiot.
               ICONIFY   = Toggle between Screen/Window.
               SLEEP     = Toggle between Sleep/Wake.
               ADDTIME   = Add time to User.
               SUBTIME   = Subtract time from User.
               FIDO<n>   = eg FIDO1, FIDO2, etc. Call FidoNet numbers 1-5
               EXEC<n>   = eg EXEC1, EXEC2, etc. Execute scripts 1-5
               IMPORT    = Force manual Message Base Import.

             eg. Control 1 SLEEP   ;Will toggle the sleep function of node 1
                 Control 2 FIDO3   ;Will dial FidoNET number 3 on node 2
                 Control 1 EXEC5   ;Will execute script number 5 for node 1

           - A full usage template is available when either the incorrect 
             number or incorrect arguments are used.

               Control   ;Will bring up the usage template.

